  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Your ID just rounded itself in JavaScript?"
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Most devs miss this."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "Above Number dot MAX SAFE INTEGER, a double cannot store every whole number, so the last digits silently change."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Send IDs as strings, or use BigInt. Then the exact value survives, every single digit. Zero digits lost."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "String IDs, or BigInt? Comment your answer."
  },
  {
   "id": "follow",
   "text": "Follow K four coding for part five."
